# Giskard Agents — Project Overview

## What is this?

`giskard-agents` is a lightweight, async-first library for orchestrating LLM completions and agent workflows. It is open-source (MIT) and designed to be approachable for new contributors.

## Core Concepts

- **Generator** — wraps a model (via LiteLLM) and exposes `.chat()` / `.template()` to build workflows.
- **ChatWorkflow** — the builder that assembles messages, tools, inputs, and output schemas, then runs completions.
- **Chat / Message** — immutable result objects returned after a workflow run.
- **Tool** — a decorated Python function the LLM can call. Defined with `@agents.tool`.
- **RunContext** — shared key-value store passed to tools during a run.
- **ErrorPolicy** — controls how errors propagate (`RAISE`, `RETURN`, `SKIP`).

## Architecture

```
src/giskard/agents/
├── generators/          # LLM backends (base ABC + LiteLLM impl)
│   ├── base.py          # BaseGenerator, GenerationParams, StreamChunk
│   ├── litellm_generator.py
│   ├── mixins.py        # Shared generator capabilities
│   └── retry.py         # Retry / back-off logic
├── tools/               # Tool system
│   ├── tool.py          # Tool, ToolCall, @tool decorator
│   └── _docstring_parser.py
├── templates/           # Jinja2 prompt templating
├── embeddings/          # Embedding model abstraction
├── errors/              # WorkflowError, serializable Error
├── workflow.py          # ChatWorkflow — the main orchestration engine
├── chat.py              # Chat & Message models
├── context.py           # RunContext
├── pipeline.py          # Low-level parallel execution
├── config.py            # Global configuration
└── rate_limiter.py      # Token / request rate limiting
```

## Key Files

- `pyproject.toml` — build config, dependencies, tooling
- `Makefile` — development workflow commands (`make help`)
- `README.md` — end-user docs with progressive examples

## Constraints

- Python >= 3.11 required
- Everything is async (`asyncio`)
- Pydantic v2 for all models
- LiteLLM as the default LLM provider
